e people to do so if you  haven't succeeded with counting calories  or counting macros for weight loss i  don't think that this is much different  it's basically the same thing but with a  better pr team plus oprah oh and it's  not free either and that brings me to  the cost now depending on your plan  you're looking at anywhere between 24.99  and 56.29 a month so for a year that  works out to almost 300 to almost 700 a  year  not even including the sign up fee for a  lot of people this is just out of reach  and it doesn't even include the food  costs now unlike learning other gentle  nutrition 101 strategies that i  discussed in my video right here there's  a huge concern that when you stop paying  for the app and the accountability  system and the point system guides you  might not have the nutrition knowledge  or skills to really transform this into  a lifestyle it's like always using a  calculator or spell check so that you  never need to learn how to do math or  write that could be an expensive  lifestyle and lastly you're paying for  unqualified coaching so according to  linkedin wwe does include some  registered dietitians on staff but the  accountability coaches available for the  premium versions of the program  don't seem to have any nutrition or  health qualifications i did some  sleuthing looking at 10 wwe coaches on  linkedin  and only one was a dietitian and she  specialized in diabetes specific cases  the other nine had backgrounds in either  sales communication or product  development obviously is it that obvious  i'm sorry now of course this is not an  official survey of the staff at ww but  from the information that i can find  publicly it doesn't seem like ww  requires their coaches to have any  official nutrition or health background  so if you're looking for a personalized  nutrition program and somebody to hold  you accountable with credentials to do  so properly i would think your money  would be much better spent investing in  an actual rd so to summarize i do think  that the new ww programs seem to offer  greater flexibility and options than  previous versions while maintaining the  kind of community and the accountability  aspects that it's been celebrated for in  the past but unless you're willing to  pay for the structure that they built  for life it may not set you up to make  healthy eating a lifestyle and maybe  that's a really good business move on  their part like why teach a man or a  woman to fish when it'll mean that they  no longer pay you to fish for them so in  conclusion while some research suggests  that wwe dieters do achieve success we  really don't know how dieters fare long  term or when they stop paying for the  service but if the data we have on  weight loss diets in general is any  indication most people will probably  gain the weight back not all but most  and of course calorie counting or pseudo  calorie counting like this  can absolutely work for some folks but i  do worry about the scarcity mentality of  a program like this so if you're looking  for more sustainable weight loss tips  that don't cost you anything to learn  definitely check out my video right here  and on that note that is all that i have  for you guys today thank you again to  squarespace for sponsoring this video  if you liked it be sure to give it the  thumbs up  leave me a comment below on other diets  that you want to see me review subscribe  to the channel and i will see you next  time on abby's kitchen  bye  [Music]
 

